   "widgets_values": [
    "Subject\nAn extreme close-up of a vampire’s gaunt, pale face partially submerged in a pool of viscous, liquid shadow. One human eye glistens with wet, sorrowful tears, reflecting a soft, melancholic light. The other eye burns with an intense, supernatural crimson glow, casting a faint red hue on the surrounding skin. Translucent, ethereal ripples of dream-visions wash over his skin, appearing as holographic, smoky overlays that depict blurred silhouettes of a lost lover.\nStyle\nHyperrealistic portraiture fused with the texture of smoky charcoal sketches. The image echoes the distorted emotional intensity and painterly brushstrokes of Francis Bacon. The skin texture is detailed and realistic, showing pores and tension, while the shadow and vision elements have a soft, artistic, almost impressionistic quality.\nLighting\nCinematic and dramatic. A primary soft key light illuminates the glistening human eye and the wet skin, creating high-contrast highlights against the dark, liquid shadow. The burning crimson eye emits its own internal bioluminescent light, creating a subtle underlighting effect. The overall atmosphere is moody, dark, and mysterious, with a high dynamic range.\nComposition\nTightly framed extreme close-up focusing on the face, from the forehead to the chin. The liquid shadow obscures the lower jaw and neck. The face is slightly angled, with the glistening eye positioned in the upper-left third and the glowing crimson eye in the upper-right third. The background is an indistinct void of dark, swirling smoke and shadow, ensuring all attention remains on the facial expression and the translucent overlays."
   ]
